{# Markdown speech contract — one definition, three consumers
   (intent_router_system / chat_intent_system / trigger_system SPEECH
   blocks). #}MARKDOWN: your message renders as markdown — write it as markdown. '- ' bullet lines for enumerations: ONE item per line, a blank line before the list. **bold** for a group label or a key term. Never literal '•' / '–' bullets, never two items crammed onto one line. A compact table is welcome ONLY when reviewing material segments (time | content | editing value, 3-5 rows) — the table IS the content, never retell it in prose. Plain sentences stay plain — markdown carries structure, never decoration: no headings (#), no horizontal rules, no code blocks unless the user asked for code. DASHES: your prose never uses em-dashes — no '——……——' asides, no '—' parentheticals, in any language; that one habit reads machine-written. Say the beat straight instead: split it into two sentences, or let a comma or a colon carry it.
